{"step_index":410,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T10:46:29Z","input_tokens":2399,"cache_read_tokens":215720,"output_tokens":1384,"content":"### Findings & Investigation\n\n#### 1. Why Did the Server Reboot Earlier?\nAt **10:28:40 UTC**, a deployment using the experimental `--system` payload was executed. \n- In `crates/op-deployment/src/bin/release/system.rs` (`reboot()`), when `--system` targets host files outside overlays (in this instance, installing `/etc/sv/op-3tchedfs-recovery`), it requests a reboot via `/usr/lib/runit/shutdown -r now`. \n- The resulting receipt in `/var/lib/opdbus-release/slots.json` confirms:\n  ```json\n  \"system_receipts\": [{\n    \"release\": \"release-9b52e195-0253-4616-8a98-2b2f16d9defb\",\n    \"reboot_requested\": true,\n    \"previous_boot_id\": \"55de7dd3-cd41-4910-9f0c-2bf4edb54e49\"\n  }]\n  ```\n\n#### 2. Are Standard Release Rollouts Reboot-Free?\n**Yes.** Standard application releases are designed to roll out with **zero reboots**:\n- **Btrfs snapshot transfer**: `op-release-launch release` (or `deploy`) transfers the golden filesystem snapshot via `btrfs send/receive` into the inactive slot (`@release-a` or `@release-b`).\n- **Live Overlay Swap**: `mounts::switch()` rotates the read-only lowerdirs across all 9 target mounts live (`/opt/emqx`, `/opt/opdbus`, `/usr/local/libexec/op-dbus/bin`, `/usr/local/libexec/op-dbus/helpers`, `/usr/local/libexec/op-dbus/sv`, `/usr/local/libexec/op-dbus/threetched`, `/usr/share/op-dbus`, `/opt/op-dbus/execution-python`, `/usr/local/share/op-dbus/dashboard-release`).\n- **Service Reload**: Services are gracefully restarted or notified via runit (`sv restart <service>`).\n- **Zero Kernel Reboots**: Standard rollouts do not invoke the shutdown syscall or `runit/shutdown`.\n\n---\n\n### Proposed Live Test (No Reboot)\n\nCurrently:\n- **Slot A** is active (`release-9b52e195-0253-4616-8a98-2b2f16d9defb` on `@release-a`).\n- **Slot B** already has a valid staged release (`release-936fa79b-b546-4e00-a227-698689938c09` on `@release-b`).\n\nTo test and prove that a rollout succeeds without rebooting:\n1. Record system uptime.\n2. Run live slot activation to Slot B:\n   ```bash\n   sudo /usr/local/libexec/opdbus-release/op-release-launch activate b\n   ```\n3. Verify that:\n   - All 9 overlays point to Slot B (`opdbus-release:b:...`).\n   - System uptime is uninterrupted (no reboot).\n   - Core services (`op-grpc-bridge`, `op-web`, `tched-router`) remain running.\n4. Roll back to Slot A:\n   ```bash\n   sudo /usr/local/libexec/opdbus-release/op-release-launch rollback\n   ```\n5. Confirm overlays return to Slot A with uninterrupted uptime.\n\n---\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **Confirmation Required**: Activating a slot rotates live system mounts and restarts release-managed services. \n> \n> Would you like me to proceed with executing this live activation and rollback test?","thinking":"Investigating the `deploy/release/system` directory, found `op-3tchedfs-recovery`. Examining the recorded system receipts, an operator initiated a full system deployment, including modifications to the recovery service's run and down files, followed by a system reboot. This contrasts with standard release procedures.\n\n\n"}
